# R8 keep rules. AGP combines every file in src/main/keepRules.
#
# Most of what this app uses ships its own consumer rules — Room, Hilt/Dagger, WorkManager,
# Compose, Glance, Play Services Ads and UMP all bundle keeps in their AARs, so none of them
# need rules here. What follows is only the things R8 cannot see, because they are resolved by
# *name* at runtime rather than by reference.

# --- Enum constant names that are persisted ---
#
# Category.name is written to the `category` column and ThemeMode.name into DataStore; both are
# read back by string-matching against `entries`. If those names were ever obfuscated, every
# stored category would silently decode to OTHER on upgrade and the saved theme would reset.
#
# In practice AGP's default proguard-android-optimize.txt already prevents that: it keeps
# values() and valueOf() on every enum, and keeping valueOf forces R8 to retain the constant
# names. Verified by removing the rules below and rebuilding — the names survived regardless.
#
# They are kept anyway, deliberately. They cost nothing, they stop this from resting on a default
# config that is outside our control, and they document that these particular names are stored
# data rather than implementation detail — which is the part a future reader would not guess.
-keepclassmembers enum dev.randyapps.lapse.data.model.Category { <fields>; }
-keepclassmembers enum dev.randyapps.lapse.data.model.QuickPick { <fields>; }
-keepclassmembers enum dev.randyapps.lapse.data.settings.ThemeMode { <fields>; }

# ItemStatus and ExpirySection are derived at read time and never stored, so they are safe to
# obfuscate. Listed here only so the next reader knows the omission is deliberate.

# --- Worker class names ---
#
# WorkManager persists the worker's fully-qualified class name in its own database and
# instantiates it by that name later. A reminder enqueued by one build is run by the next, so a
# name that changed between releases would leave scheduled reminders unable to start — silently,
# and only for users who upgrade. androidx.work ships a consumer rule covering ListenableWorker
# subclasses; as with the enums, these are explicit so the guarantee is ours and not inherited.
-keep class dev.randyapps.lapse.notifications.ReminderWorker { *; }
-keep class dev.randyapps.lapse.widget.DailyWidgetRefreshWorker { *; }

# --- Glance widget ---
#
# The receiver is named in the manifest and so is kept automatically, but the GlanceAppWidget it
# returns is also reconstructed when the system restores widget state.
-keep class dev.randyapps.lapse.widget.NextExpiryWidget { *; }
-keep class dev.randyapps.lapse.widget.NextExpiryWidgetReceiver { *; }
